   "title": "Savage Highlands",
   "text": "Skip to Content\nAccessibility Information\nAn official website of the State of Maryland. Here's how you know\nMaryland State Jobs\nTranslate\nSearch\nSearch\nFind a State Park\nPark Activities & Amenities\nCamping, Cabins and Shelters\nDNR Home\nMARYLAND DEPARTMENT OF NATURAL RESOURCES\nMARYLAND PARK SERVICE\nSavage Highlands State Park\nHighlights\n​\n​​\n​\nSection3\n​​ ​​​​​​\nAbout the Park\n​\n​Savage Highlands is located about ten miles west of Frostburg, MD, near the Allegh​any Front and Eastern Continental Divide in Garrett County. It is securely positioned within the westernmost reaches of the Chesapeake Bay watershed, despite being perched over 2500 ft in elevation on Big Savage Mountain. The surrounding Mt. Aetna Tract of Savage River State Forest allows for about eight miles of non-motorized, multi-use trails​. Hiking, mountain biking, cross country skiing, snowshoeing and picnicking can be accommodated from the state park.\n​Hunting opportunities and fishing in the Savage River are accessible nearby from the adjacent Savage River State Forest. Wildlife enthusiasts may see white tailed deer, black bear, bobcats, birds-of-prey, and a variety of song birds and reptiles while exploring the property. Guests are encouraged to practice Leave No Trace outdoor ethics​ to minimize their impact on the surrounding resources and avoid any potential for negative wildlife interactions.\n​\nT​he Highlands Lodge\n​\n​The Lodge at Savage Highlands State Park, located at 1600 Mt. Aetna Rd, Frostburg, MD 2153​2, will serve as the central hub for information, reservations, and other visitor services. Amenities include public WiFi, restrooms, ADA access​, a large, indoor wood burning fireplace, an extensive collection of books and games, and cozy indoor and outdoor seating.\nThe Lodge is open daily, from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m. April through October. Currently, there is no food service at the Lodge, as the kitchen is being renovated.\n​\n​\n​​​\n​​ ​​​​​​\nRecreational Activities​​\n​\nHiking\n​Access approximately six miles of moderately challenging multi-use trails within Savage River State Forest (Mt. Aetna Tract). Visitors should be prepared for natural hazards (poison ivy, slippery surfaces) and plan responsibly.​\n​ ​​ ​​​Trail Descr​iptions​​​\n​\n​ ​​\n​\nWildlife\n​\nExploring the high-country trails offers wildlife enthusiasts the chance to spot black bears, bobcats, coyotes, and white-tailed deer, alongside birds of prey, songbirds, snakes and turtles. ​Observing or encountering wildlife is a common experience around Savage Highlands State Park. Visitors are encouraged to follow Leave No Trace Outdoor Ethics and respect wildlife by providing ample distance between you and the animal, and refraining from feeding, handling or harassing wildlife in any way, including keeping pets on a leash. It is important not to interfere with wildlife’s natural instincts and abilities to thrive in their habitat.\n​​​​\n​\nSection2\nStay with us at Savage Highlands​. Rent a yurt​\n​\nQueen Bed and Full Bathroom​​\nDesigned for ultimate comfort, this modern yurt features a luxurious queen-size bed set beneath the central dome, allowing you to gaze up at the night sky from the warmth of high-end linens. Just steps away, a fully enclosed private bathroom seamlessly blends rustic charm with upscale convenience, complete with a dual-basin sink vanity and a spacious full-sized walk-in shower. This unique setup offers all the immersive tranquility of a traditional circular retreat without sacrificing the essential luxuries and convenience of a high-end hotel suite.\n​​\nFull Size Living Area\nAnchoring the interior of the yurt is an expansive, open-concept living space designed for effortless relaxation, featuring a plush leather couch, comfortable accent chairs, and a rustic coffee table ideal for morning coffee or late-night board games. Large windows flood the circular room with natural light, while double glass doors open directly onto a private covered porch. Step outside to take in the surrounding forest views, unwind in the fresh mountain air, or seamlessly transition between indoor comfort and outdoor serenity throughout your stay.\n​\n​​​\nKitchen Area​​\nThe yurt features a thoughtfully equipped kitchenette, complete with a sink, mini-refrigerator, microwave, coffee maker, and a full set of mugs for your morning brew. Adjacent to the counter space is a cozy breakfast nook, offering a bright, intimate spot to savor casual meals, plan your day's outdoor adventures, or simply enjoy a quiet cup of coffee with a view. Outdoor picnic tables and charcoal grills are planned for 2027.\nTo make a reservation click here.\nMORE PHOTOS​​\n​​\n​\nStay with us at Savage Highlands. Coming soon, cabins​\n​\nNot so rustic cabins​​\nDiscover the timeless allure of a rugged log cabin combined with surprising comfort. While our cabin’s traditional chinked log exterior and weathered porch, blend perfectly into the dense, natural woodland of one of Maryland's largest state forests, a look inside reveals a posh sanctuary designed for discerning guests. Enjoy the quintessential mountain adventure by day, exploring pristine trails and scenic vistas, then return to a refined interior that offers all the plush comforts of a hotel stay, all while maintaining the serene seclusion of our beautiful state park setting.\n​​\nFull Size Living Area\nStep inside and experience the seamless harmony of wilderness charm and refined comfort, where warm, exposed timber beams and handcrafted log walls envelop an inviting, spacious living area. Tucked deep within the serene wilderness of Savage River State Forest, this mountain sanctuary offers plush, comfortable seating centered around a handcrafted wood coffee table, richly textured floors, and generous natural light streaming through the windows. Whether you are unwinding after a day on the forest trails or quietly sinking into a cozy armchair with a good book, this inviting interior brings high-end relaxation directly to your rugged, off-the-grid retreat.\n​\n​​​\nLoft master bedroom​\nPerched beneath the soaring vaulted ceilings of the cabin’s A-frame, this open master loft serves as an elevated private sanctuary wrapped entirely in warm, natural timber. Dramatic, heavy-timber rafters frame a plush, inviting bed flanked by classic nightstands and soft ambient lamps, creating a cozy sleeping nook bathed in natural wood tones. Overseen by a classic ceiling fan and protected by a rustic wooden railing with wrought-iron balusters, this airy retreat overlooks the main living space below while offering guests an intimate, treetop slumber experience in the heart of the forest.​\nMORE PHOTOS​​​\n​​\n​\nWhy Savage Highlands Became a State Park\n​\nSavage Highlands became a state park to ensure this ecologically significant mountain landscape is stewarded for the long term and remains compatible with the surrounding Savage River State Forest trail and recreation network. The property is a significant inholding within Savage River State Forest. A change in use by a private owner could have fragmented the landscape, disrupted interconnected trail systems, and undermined long-term conservation goals for the broader tract of public land.​\nIt also expands public overnight opportunities in Western Maryland, where cabins, campsites, and park lodging are often at capacity, by converting an existing lodge-and-cabin property into a family-friendly state park rather than building a new facility from scratch. The site offered substantial existing infrastructure, including cabins, yurts, trails, utilities, and a lodge that, while in need of upgrades, provided a rare opportunity to convert a pre-existing facility into a state park. Building a comparable park entirely from scratch would require capital investments several times higher than the purchase price and renovation costs.​​\nHuman Trafficking GET HELP\nNational Human Trafficking Hotline - 24/7 Confidential\n1-888-373-7888\n233733\nMore Information\non human trafficking in Maryland\nMission Statement​\nThe Department of Natural Resources leads Maryland in securing a sustainable future for our environment, society, and economy by preserving, protecting, restoring, and enhancing the State’s natural resources.\nLearn More About DNR\nHelp Stop Fraud in State Government\nThe Maryland General Assembly’s Office of Legislative Audits operates a toll-free fraud hotline to receive allegations of fraud and/or abuse of State government resources. Information reported to the hotline in the past has helped to eliminate certain fraudulent activities and protect State resources.\nMore Information\n© Copyright Maryland.gov. All rights reserved.\nContact Us Privacy & Security Accessibility More Online Services Website Feedback Register to Vote Nondiscrimination / No discriminación\n580 Taylor Ave., Annapolis, MD 21401\nCall toll-free in *Maryland* at 1-877-620-8DNR (8367)\nOut of State: 410-260-8DNR (8367)\nBanner Photo: Sandy Point State Park - Photo: Carmelita Woy",
